.TH SDL_HINT_VIDEO_MATCH_EXCLUSIVE_MODE_ON_MOVE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_VIDEO_MATCH_EXCLUSIVE_MODE_ON_MOVE \- A variable controlling whether SDL will attempt to automatically set the destination display to a mode most closely matching that of the previous display if an exclusive fullscreen window is moved onto it.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_MATCH_EXCLUSIVE_MODE_ON_MOVE \(dqSDL_VIDEO_MATCH_EXCLUSIVE_MODE_ON_MOVE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: SDL will not attempt to automatically set a matching mode on the destination display\[char46] If an exclusive fullscreen window is moved to a new display, the window will become fullscreen desktop\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: SDL will attempt to automatically set a mode on the destination display that most closely matches the mode of the display that the exclusive fullscreen window was previously on\[char46] (default)
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

